3,"Kulango, Bouna in Côte d'Ivoire - Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/10955/IV,"The Kulango speak Kulango Bouna (or Nkurange), a Gur language from the Niger Congo language family. The Kulango are closely related to the Lobi, their former enemies. The two groups occupy the same region and share similar languages, customs, religious beliefs and lifestyles. What Are Their Lives Like?","Kulango, Bouna",Niger-Congo
